        "format": "plain_text",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.tooltip()",
        "text": "Kind is a type of metadata that is used to classify prims in USD and determines the selection behavior in the Viewport. Custom strings can be defined for production pipelines.\nKind examples:<ul><li>assembly - an important group model, often a published asset or reference to a published asset</li><li>group - models that simply group other models.</li><li>component - a 'leaf model' that can contain no other models</li><li>model - base class for all model kinds. 'model' is considered an abstract type and should not be assigned as any prim's kind.</li><li>subcomponent - an identified, important 'sub part' of a component model.</li></ul>"
      },
